			<item>
				<title>Cloud Native Quick Reference</title>
				<link>https://samirsahoo.github.io/cloud-native/self-review/quick-reference/</link>
				<pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid>https://samirsahoo.github.io/cloud-native/self-review/quick-reference/</guid>
				<description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;kubernetes-objects-at-a-glance&#34;&gt;Kubernetes objects at a glance&lt;a class=&#34;heading-anchor&#34; href=&#34;#kubernetes-objects-at-a-glance&#34; aria-label=&#34;Link to this section&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;table-wrap&#34; tabindex=&#34;0&#34; role=&#34;region&#34; aria-label=&#34;Table&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;table&gt;&#xA;  &lt;thead&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;th&gt;Need&lt;/th&gt;&#xA;      &lt;th&gt;Object&lt;/th&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/thead&gt;&#xA;  &lt;tbody&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Stateless app&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Deployment (+ HPA, PDB)&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Stateful app&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;StatefulSet + PVC (or operator / managed service)&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Per-node agent&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;DaemonSet&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Batch / scheduled&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Job / CronJob&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Stable address&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Service&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;North-south traffic&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Gateway + HTTPRoute&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Config / secrets&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;ConfigMap / Secret (+ External Secrets)&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Isolation &amp;amp; budgets&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Namespace, ResourceQuota, LimitRange, NetworkPolicy&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Availability during drains&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;PodDisruptionBudget&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;New API types&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;CRD + operator&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/tbody&gt;&#xA;&lt;/table&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;kubectl-essentials&#34;&gt;kubectl essentials&lt;a class=&#34;heading-anchor&#34; href=&#34;#kubectl-essentials&#34; aria-label=&#34;Link to this section&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-bash&#34; data-lang=&#34;bash&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;kubectl get pods -n shop -o wide            &lt;span class=&#34;c1&#34;&gt;# what is running where&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;kubectl describe pod &amp;lt;pod&amp;gt; -n shop          &lt;span class=&#34;c1&#34;&gt;# events and reasons&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;kubectl logs deploy/orders -n shop -f       &lt;span class=&#34;c1&#34;&gt;# logs&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;kubectl events -n shop --types&lt;span class=&#34;o&#34;&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;Warning      &lt;span class=&#34;c1&#34;&gt;# recent problems&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;kubectl diff -f k8s/                        &lt;span class=&#34;c1&#34;&gt;# preview changes&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;kubectl rollout status deploy/orders        &lt;span class=&#34;c1&#34;&gt;# watch a rollout&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;kubectl rollout undo deploy/orders          &lt;span class=&#34;c1&#34;&gt;# roll back&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;kubectl debug -it &amp;lt;pod&amp;gt; --image&lt;span class=&#34;o&#34;&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;busybox     &lt;span class=&#34;c1&#34;&gt;# ephemeral debug container&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;kubectl auth can-i delete pods --as&lt;span class=&#34;o&#34;&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;jane    &lt;span class=&#34;c1&#34;&gt;# check RBAC&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;kubectl top pods -n shop                    &lt;span class=&#34;c1&#34;&gt;# resource usage&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2 id=&#34;secure-defaults&#34;&gt;Secure defaults&lt;a class=&#34;heading-anchor&#34; href=&#34;#secure-defaults&#34; aria-label=&#34;Link to this section&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;table-wrap&#34; tabindex=&#34;0&#34; role=&#34;region&#34; aria-label=&#34;Table&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;table&gt;&#xA;  &lt;thead&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;th&gt;Area&lt;/th&gt;&#xA;      &lt;th&gt;Default&lt;/th&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/thead&gt;&#xA;  &lt;tbody&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Pod security&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Namespace label &lt;code&gt;pod-security.kubernetes.io/enforce: restricted&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Container&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;non-root, read-only root FS, drop ALL capabilities, seccomp RuntimeDefault&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Network&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Default-deny NetworkPolicy + explicit allows (incl. DNS)&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Images&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Minimal base, scanned, signed, SBOM, deployed by digest&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Secrets&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;External store + External Secrets Operator; etcd encryption at rest&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Access&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;OIDC humans, least-privilege RBAC, read-only prod, workload identity for Pods&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/tbody&gt;&#xA;&lt;/table&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;delivery&#34;&gt;Delivery&lt;a class=&#34;heading-anchor&#34; href=&#34;#delivery&#34; aria-label=&#34;Link to this section&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;table-wrap&#34; tabindex=&#34;0&#34; role=&#34;region&#34; aria-label=&#34;Table&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;table&gt;&#xA;  &lt;thead&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;th&gt;Topic&lt;/th&gt;&#xA;      &lt;th&gt;Rule of thumb&lt;/th&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/thead&gt;&#xA;  &lt;tbody&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Artifacts&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Build once, sign, promote by digest&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Packaging&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Helm for packages, Kustomize for overlays&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Deployment&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;GitOps pull (Argo CD / Flux); folders per environment, not branches&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Rollout&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Canary with automated analysis (Argo Rollouts / Flagger)&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Secrets in Git&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Never plaintext: External Secrets, Sealed Secrets or SOPS&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Governance&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Risk-based automated approvals; orchestration for multi-team releases&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;DORA&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Deploy frequency, lead time, change failure rate, recovery time&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/tbody&gt;&#xA;&lt;/table&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;platform-engineering&#34;&gt;Platform engineering&lt;a class=&#34;heading-anchor&#34; href=&#34;#platform-engineering&#34; aria-label=&#34;Link to this section&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;table-wrap&#34; tabindex=&#34;0&#34; role=&#34;region&#34; aria-label=&#34;Table&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;table&gt;&#xA;  &lt;thead&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;th&gt;Concept&lt;/th&gt;&#xA;      &lt;th&gt;One-liner&lt;/th&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/thead&gt;&#xA;  &lt;tbody&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Platform as a product&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Developers are customers; adoption is earned&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Golden path&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Opinionated supported route with guardrails&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;IDP planes&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Developer control, integration &amp;amp; delivery, resources, observability, security&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Portal&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Backstage: catalog, templates, TechDocs, plugins&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Infra APIs&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Crossplane / kro claims and compositions&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;DevEx&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Feedback loops, cognitive load, flow state&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Maturity aspects&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Investment, adoption, interfaces, operations, measurement&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/tbody&gt;&#xA;&lt;/table&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;slo-maths&#34;&gt;SLO maths&lt;a class=&#34;heading-anchor&#34; href=&#34;#slo-maths&#34; aria-label=&#34;Link to this section&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;table-wrap&#34; tabindex=&#34;0&#34; role=&#34;region&#34; aria-label=&#34;Table&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;table&gt;&#xA;  &lt;thead&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;th&gt;SLO&lt;/th&gt;&#xA;      &lt;th&gt;Downtime / 30 days&lt;/th&gt;&#xA;      &lt;th&gt;Error budget&lt;/th&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/thead&gt;&#xA;  &lt;tbody&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;99%&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;7.2 h&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;1%&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;99.5%&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;3.6 h&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;0.5%&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;99.9%&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;43 min&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;0.1%&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;99.95%&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;22 min&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;0.05%&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;99.99%&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;4.3 min&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;0.01%&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/tbody&gt;&#xA;&lt;/table&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Fast-burn page (99.9% SLO): burn rate ≥ 14.4 over 1 h and 5 min = 2% of monthly budget in one hour.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>About this handbook</title>
				<link>https://samirsahoo.github.io/cloud-native/about/</link>
				<pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid>https://samirsahoo.github.io/cloud-native/about/</guid>
				<description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;purpose&#34;&gt;Purpose&lt;a class=&#34;heading-anchor&#34; href=&#34;#purpose&#34; aria-label=&#34;Link to this section&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The &lt;strong&gt;Cloud Native &amp;amp; Platform Engineering Knowledge Hub&lt;/strong&gt; explains how modern platforms are built and run — simply, with diagrams and flows — for architects, platform engineers, SREs and developers. It is the companion to the &lt;a href=&#34;https://samirsahoo.github.io/design-patterns-hub/&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;Java &amp;amp; Software Architecture Knowledge Hub&lt;/a&gt; and the &lt;a href=&#34;https://samirsahoo.github.io/enterprise-ai/&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;Enterprise AI &amp;amp; Agentic AI Knowledge Hub&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>Glossary</title>
				<link>https://samirsahoo.github.io/cloud-native/glossary/</link>
				<pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid>https://samirsahoo.github.io/cloud-native/glossary/</guid>
				<description>&lt;p&gt;Definitions are deliberately short. Follow the links for the full explanation.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3 id=&#34;ac&#34;&gt;A–C&lt;a class=&#34;heading-anchor&#34; href=&#34;#ac&#34; aria-label=&#34;Link to this section&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;dl&gt;&#xA;&lt;dt&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Admission control&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/dt&gt;&#xA;&lt;dd&gt;Checks that validate or mutate API objects before they are stored. See &lt;a href=&#34;https://samirsahoo.github.io/cloud-native/kubernetes/kubernetes-security/&#34;&gt;Kubernetes security&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/dd&gt;&#xA;&lt;dt&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Argo CD&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/dt&gt;&#xA;&lt;dd&gt;A GitOps controller that syncs Kubernetes clusters with Git. See &lt;a href=&#34;https://samirsahoo.github.io/cloud-native/delivery/gitops/#argo-cd&#34;&gt;GitOps&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/dd&gt;&#xA;&lt;dt&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Argo Rollouts&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/dt&gt;&#xA;&lt;dd&gt;Progressive delivery controller for canary and blue-green rollouts. See &lt;a href=&#34;https://samirsahoo.github.io/cloud-native/delivery/ci-cd-pipelines/#deployment-strategies&#34;&gt;CI/CD&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/dd&gt;&#xA;&lt;dt&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Backstage&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/dt&gt;&#xA;&lt;dd&gt;An open-source developer portal framework (catalog, templates, docs, plugins). See &lt;a href=&#34;https://samirsahoo.github.io/cloud-native/platform-engineering/internal-developer-platforms/#the-developer-portal-backstage&#34;&gt;IDPs&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/dd&gt;&#xA;&lt;dt&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Blue-green deployment&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/dt&gt;&#xA;&lt;dd&gt;Switching all traffic between two complete environments. See &lt;a href=&#34;https://samirsahoo.github.io/cloud-native/delivery/ci-cd-pipelines/#deployment-strategies&#34;&gt;CI/CD&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/dd&gt;&#xA;&lt;dt&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Burn rate&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/dt&gt;&#xA;&lt;dd&gt;How fast an error budget is being consumed relative to the SLO. See &lt;a href=&#34;https://samirsahoo.github.io/cloud-native/sre/sre-fundamentals/#burn-rate-alerting&#34;&gt;SRE&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/dd&gt;&#xA;&lt;dt&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Canary release&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/dt&gt;&#xA;&lt;dd&gt;Gradually shifting traffic to a new version while analysing metrics. See &lt;a href=&#34;https://samirsahoo.github.io/cloud-native/delivery/ci-cd-pipelines/#deployment-strategies&#34;&gt;CI/CD&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/dd&gt;&#xA;&lt;dt&gt;&lt;strong&gt;cgroups&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/dt&gt;&#xA;&lt;dd&gt;Linux control groups that limit a process&amp;rsquo;s resources. See &lt;a href=&#34;https://samirsahoo.github.io/cloud-native/delivery/containers-and-docker/#how-it-works&#34;&gt;Containers&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/dd&gt;&#xA;&lt;dt&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CNI / CRI / CSI&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/dt&gt;&#xA;&lt;dd&gt;Standard interfaces for networking, container runtimes and storage. See &lt;a href=&#34;https://samirsahoo.github.io/cloud-native/kubernetes/kubernetes-architecture/&#34;&gt;Architecture&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/dd&gt;&#xA;&lt;dt&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Crossplane&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/dt&gt;&#xA;&lt;dd&gt;A Kubernetes-based control plane for provisioning infrastructure through APIs. See &lt;a href=&#34;https://samirsahoo.github.io/cloud-native/platform-engineering/internal-developer-platforms/#infrastructure-as-apis&#34;&gt;IDPs&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/dd&gt;&#xA;&lt;dt&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Custom resource / operator&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/dt&gt;&#xA;&lt;dd&gt;A new API type and the controller that automates it. See &lt;a href=&#34;https://samirsahoo.github.io/cloud-native/kubernetes/kubernetes-architecture/#extending-kubernetes&#34;&gt;Architecture&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/dd&gt;&#xA;&lt;/dl&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3 id=&#34;dg&#34;&gt;D–G&lt;a class=&#34;heading-anchor&#34; href=&#34;#dg&#34; aria-label=&#34;Link to this section&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;dl&gt;&#xA;&lt;dt&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Developer experience (DevEx)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/dt&gt;&#xA;&lt;dd&gt;How developers perceive their work environment: feedback loops, cognitive load, flow. See &lt;a href=&#34;https://samirsahoo.github.io/cloud-native/platform-engineering/developer-experience/&#34;&gt;DevEx&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/dd&gt;&#xA;&lt;dt&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Digital.ai Release / Deploy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/dt&gt;&#xA;&lt;dd&gt;Enterprise release orchestration and model-driven deployment tools. See &lt;a href=&#34;https://samirsahoo.github.io/cloud-native/delivery/release-orchestration/&#34;&gt;Release orchestration&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/dd&gt;&#xA;&lt;dt&gt;&lt;strong&gt;DORA metrics&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/dt&gt;&#xA;&lt;dd&gt;Deployment frequency, lead time, change failure rate, recovery time. See &lt;a href=&#34;https://samirsahoo.github.io/cloud-native/delivery/ci-cd-pipelines/#measuring-delivery-dora-metrics&#34;&gt;CI/CD&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/dd&gt;&#xA;&lt;dt&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dynamic Resource Allocation (DRA)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/dt&gt;&#xA;&lt;dd&gt;Kubernetes API for requesting GPUs and other devices. See &lt;a href=&#34;https://samirsahoo.github.io/cloud-native/kubernetes/workloads-and-scheduling/#scheduling-controls&#34;&gt;Workloads&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/dd&gt;&#xA;&lt;dt&gt;&lt;strong&gt;eBPF&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/dt&gt;&#xA;&lt;dd&gt;Programs running safely in the Linux kernel, used for networking, security and observability. See &lt;a href=&#34;https://samirsahoo.github.io/cloud-native/kubernetes/kubernetes-networking/&#34;&gt;Networking&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/dd&gt;&#xA;&lt;dt&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Error budget&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/dt&gt;&#xA;&lt;dd&gt;The allowed unreliability, 1 − SLO. See &lt;a href=&#34;https://samirsahoo.github.io/cloud-native/sre/sre-fundamentals/#error-budgets&#34;&gt;SRE&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/dd&gt;&#xA;&lt;dt&gt;&lt;strong&gt;etcd&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/dt&gt;&#xA;&lt;dd&gt;The distributed key-value store holding Kubernetes state. See &lt;a href=&#34;https://samirsahoo.github.io/cloud-native/kubernetes/kubernetes-architecture/#control-plane&#34;&gt;Architecture&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/dd&gt;&#xA;&lt;dt&gt;&lt;strong&gt;FinOps&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/dt&gt;&#xA;&lt;dd&gt;Practice of managing cloud value through engineering–finance collaboration. See &lt;a href=&#34;https://samirsahoo.github.io/cloud-native/sre/finops/&#34;&gt;FinOps&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/dd&gt;&#xA;&lt;dt&gt;&lt;strong&gt;FOCUS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/dt&gt;&#xA;&lt;dd&gt;FinOps Open Cost and Usage Specification for billing data. See &lt;a href=&#34;https://samirsahoo.github.io/cloud-native/sre/finops/#focus-one-billing-format&#34;&gt;FinOps&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/dd&gt;&#xA;&lt;dt&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Gateway API&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/dt&gt;&#xA;&lt;dd&gt;The successor to Ingress for routing traffic into and within clusters. See &lt;a href=&#34;https://samirsahoo.github.io/cloud-native/kubernetes/kubernetes-networking/#getting-traffic-in-ingress--gateway-api&#34;&gt;Networking&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/dd&gt;&#xA;&lt;dt&gt;&lt;strong&gt;GitOps&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/dt&gt;&#xA;&lt;dd&gt;Declarative desired state in Git, pulled and reconciled by agents. See &lt;a href=&#34;https://samirsahoo.github.io/cloud-native/delivery/gitops/&#34;&gt;GitOps&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/dd&gt;&#xA;&lt;dt&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Golden path&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/dt&gt;&#xA;&lt;dd&gt;An opinionated, supported way to perform a common task. See &lt;a href=&#34;https://samirsahoo.github.io/cloud-native/platform-engineering/platform-engineering-fundamentals/#golden-paths-and-guardrails&#34;&gt;Platform engineering&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/dd&gt;&#xA;&lt;/dl&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3 id=&#34;ho&#34;&gt;H–O&lt;a class=&#34;heading-anchor&#34; href=&#34;#ho&#34; aria-label=&#34;Link to this section&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;dl&gt;&#xA;&lt;dt&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Helm&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/dt&gt;&#xA;&lt;dd&gt;The Kubernetes package manager (charts, values, releases). See &lt;a href=&#34;https://samirsahoo.github.io/cloud-native/delivery/helm-charts/&#34;&gt;Helm&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/dd&gt;&#xA;&lt;dt&gt;&lt;strong&gt;HPA / VPA / KEDA&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/dt&gt;&#xA;&lt;dd&gt;Autoscalers for replicas, requests and event-driven scaling. See &lt;a href=&#34;https://samirsahoo.github.io/cloud-native/kubernetes/workloads-and-scheduling/#autoscaling&#34;&gt;Workloads&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/dd&gt;&#xA;&lt;dt&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Internal developer platform (IDP)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/dt&gt;&#xA;&lt;dd&gt;Integrated tools, APIs and golden paths for self-service delivery. See &lt;a href=&#34;https://samirsahoo.github.io/cloud-native/platform-engineering/internal-developer-platforms/&#34;&gt;IDPs&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/dd&gt;&#xA;&lt;dt&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Karpenter&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/dt&gt;&#xA;&lt;dd&gt;A node autoscaler that provisions right-sized nodes and consolidates. See &lt;a href=&#34;https://samirsahoo.github.io/cloud-native/kubernetes/workloads-and-scheduling/#autoscaling&#34;&gt;Workloads&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/dd&gt;&#xA;&lt;dt&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Kyverno&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/dt&gt;&#xA;&lt;dd&gt;A Kubernetes-native policy engine. See &lt;a href=&#34;https://samirsahoo.github.io/cloud-native/kubernetes/kubernetes-security/#policy-as-code&#34;&gt;Security&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/dd&gt;&#xA;&lt;dt&gt;&lt;strong&gt;NetworkPolicy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/dt&gt;&#xA;&lt;dd&gt;Rules restricting Pod traffic. See &lt;a href=&#34;https://samirsahoo.github.io/cloud-native/kubernetes/kubernetes-networking/#network-policies-default-deny&#34;&gt;Networking&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/dd&gt;&#xA;&lt;dt&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Observability&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/dt&gt;&#xA;&lt;dd&gt;Ability to understand system behaviour from telemetry. See &lt;a href=&#34;https://samirsahoo.github.io/cloud-native/sre/observability/&#34;&gt;Observability&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/dd&gt;&#xA;&lt;dt&gt;&lt;strong&gt;OpenShift&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/dt&gt;&#xA;&lt;dd&gt;Red Hat&amp;rsquo;s enterprise Kubernetes platform. See &lt;a href=&#34;https://samirsahoo.github.io/cloud-native/delivery/openshift/&#34;&gt;OpenShift&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/dd&gt;&#xA;&lt;dt&gt;&lt;strong&gt;OpenTelemetry (OTel)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/dt&gt;&#xA;&lt;dd&gt;The vendor-neutral standard for telemetry. See &lt;a href=&#34;https://samirsahoo.github.io/cloud-native/sre/observability/#opentelemetry&#34;&gt;Observability&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/dd&gt;&#xA;&lt;/dl&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3 id=&#34;pz&#34;&gt;P–Z&lt;a class=&#34;heading-anchor&#34; href=&#34;#pz&#34; aria-label=&#34;Link to this section&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;dl&gt;&#xA;&lt;dt&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PodDisruptionBudget (PDB)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/dt&gt;&#xA;&lt;dd&gt;Limits voluntary disruptions to an application. See &lt;a href=&#34;https://samirsahoo.github.io/cloud-native/sre/resilience-and-dr/#kubernetes-resilience-features&#34;&gt;Resilience&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/dd&gt;&#xA;&lt;dt&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pod Security Standards&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/dt&gt;&#xA;&lt;dd&gt;Privileged, baseline and restricted security profiles. See &lt;a href=&#34;https://samirsahoo.github.io/cloud-native/kubernetes/kubernetes-security/#pod-security&#34;&gt;Security&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/dd&gt;&#xA;&lt;dt&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RBAC&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/dt&gt;&#xA;&lt;dd&gt;Role-based access control for the Kubernetes API. See &lt;a href=&#34;https://samirsahoo.github.io/cloud-native/kubernetes/kubernetes-security/#identity-and-access&#34;&gt;Security&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/dd&gt;&#xA;&lt;dt&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RPO / RTO&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/dt&gt;&#xA;&lt;dd&gt;Maximum acceptable data loss and downtime. See &lt;a href=&#34;https://samirsahoo.github.io/cloud-native/sre/resilience-and-dr/#rpo-and-rto&#34;&gt;Resilience&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/dd&gt;&#xA;&lt;dt&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SBOM&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/dt&gt;&#xA;&lt;dd&gt;Software bill of materials. See &lt;a href=&#34;https://samirsahoo.github.io/cloud-native/kubernetes/kubernetes-security/#supply-chain-security&#34;&gt;Security&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/dd&gt;&#xA;&lt;dt&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Service mesh&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/dt&gt;&#xA;&lt;dd&gt;Infrastructure layer for mTLS, traffic control and telemetry. See &lt;a href=&#34;https://samirsahoo.github.io/cloud-native/kubernetes/service-mesh/&#34;&gt;Service mesh&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/dd&gt;&#xA;&lt;dt&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SLI / SLO / SLA&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/dt&gt;&#xA;&lt;dd&gt;Indicator, objective and agreement for reliability. See &lt;a href=&#34;https://samirsahoo.github.io/cloud-native/sre/sre-fundamentals/#sli-slo-sla&#34;&gt;SRE&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/dd&gt;&#xA;&lt;dt&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SLSA&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/dt&gt;&#xA;&lt;dd&gt;Supply-chain Levels for Software Artifacts — build provenance framework. See &lt;a href=&#34;https://samirsahoo.github.io/cloud-native/kubernetes/kubernetes-security/#supply-chain-security&#34;&gt;Security&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/dd&gt;&#xA;&lt;dt&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team Topologies&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/dt&gt;&#xA;&lt;dd&gt;Model of team types and interactions. See &lt;a href=&#34;https://samirsahoo.github.io/cloud-native/platform-engineering/platform-engineering-fundamentals/#team-topologies&#34;&gt;Platform engineering&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/dd&gt;&#xA;&lt;dt&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Toil&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/dt&gt;&#xA;&lt;dd&gt;Manual, repetitive, automatable operational work. See &lt;a href=&#34;https://samirsahoo.github.io/cloud-native/sre/sre-fundamentals/#toil-and-automation&#34;&gt;SRE&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/dd&gt;&#xA;&lt;/dl&gt;</description>
			</item>
